hpc:Job a owl:Class .
hpc:DefaultBlockAllocationMethod a owl:ObjectProperty .
hpc:MinimizeSocketsUsed a owl:ObjectProperty .
hpc:Node a owl:Class .
hpc:Socket a owl:Class .
hpc:CPU a owl:Class .
hpc:Task a owl:Class .
hpc:AllocationMethod a owl:EnumClass ;
  rdfs:member hpc:BlockAllocationMethod .
hpc:DistributionMethod a owl:EnumClass ;
  rdfs:member hpc:CyclicDistribution .
  rdfs:member hpc:PlaneDistribution .

hpc:DefaultPartition a owl:Class .
hpc:Partition a owl:Class .

hpc:AllocatedOnNode rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job ;
  rdfs:range hpc:Node .
hpc:HasAllocationMethod rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasCyclicDistribution rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasDefaultPartition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasPlaneDistribution rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasNumberOfAllocatedCPUs rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasNumberOfTasks rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasNumberOfNodes rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasNumberOfSockets rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasNumberOfCPUsPerTask rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:HasNumberOfTasksPerNode rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain hpc:Job .

hpc:NodeName a xsd:string .
hpc:SocketID a xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
hpc:NumberOfAllocatedCPUs a xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
hpc:NumberOfTasks a xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
hpc:DistributionOfTasksToNodes a xsd:string .
```

This ontology fragment represents the classes `Job`, `Node`, `Socket`, `CPU`, and `Task`, as well as properties related to job allocation, such as `AllocatedOnNode`, `HasAllocationMethod`, `HasCyclicDistribution`, `HasPlaneDistribution`, `HasNumberOfAllocatedCPUs`, `HasNumberOfTasks`, `HasNumberOfNodes`, `HasNumberOfSockets`, `HasNumberOfCPUsPerTask`, and `HasNumberOfTasksPerNode`. The datatypes used are `xsd:string` for `NodeName` and `xsd:nonNegativeInteger` for the rest.
